id: pmc-redos-startup-231
title: ReDoS validation workers time out before parser execution on busy hosts
description: "The unchanged full release gate on the merged resolution-prose branch ran 599 tests: 588 passed and all 11 ReDoS probes failed with worker did not start within 5000ms. Heavy shared-host load may have delayed module startup before the already-loaded parser CPU budget could be measured. Existing pmc-zoqj addressed operation CPU timing and descheduling; this follow-up concerns startup readiness. Keep the 250ms parser CPU budget and independently bounded hang detection; reproduce under loaded and unloaded validation conditions before proposing a separate harness change."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: performance,tests,validation
created_at: "2026-10-11T05:46:21.190Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T18:36:06.415Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Preserve every hostile input and assertion, the 250ms CPU budget and independent hang detection; demonstrate startup handling under loaded and unloaded conditions; keep any fix separate from PR 231."
repro_steps: "Run npm run release:check unchanged while the shared validation host is heavily loaded; inspect generator-redos worker startup errors."
expected_result: Parser probes reach readiness and enforce their CPU and hang budgets without treating scheduler-delayed module startup as parser failure.
actual_result: All 11 workers failed the 5000ms startup deadline in the npm release gate; no operation CPU-budget failure was reported.
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-11T06:35:53.252Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed unchanged full-gate receipts on merged head c8e7c037db23e9b10ac43a77603836d309de5871: npm 599 tests / 588 pass / 11 fail; Bun 599 / 589 / 10; fresh HOME with global and system Git config disabled 599 / 588 / 11. All failures are worker did not start within 5000ms, before the parser operation budget is measured; every run has 0 cancelled/skipped/todo. One Bun extract-release probe passed its unchanged budgets. Heavy shared-host load was observed during validation. Existing pmc-zoqj covers operation CPU timing, not this startup readiness failure. No production implementation, timeout or coverage threshold change is included here; this follow-up remains open for separate investigation."
  "2026-10-11T09:57:53.737Z",claude-hub,"Wording qualified per review: host load is a hypothesis until the loaded/unloaded comparison in the acceptance criteria exists."
  "2026-10-14T11:37:30.865Z",codex-agent,"Additional maintenance evidence: the unchanged npm release gate passed 598 of 599 tests, with only summary-format failing worker readiness at the existing 5000 ms deadline during overlapping package gates. The same named test passed in isolation (1 of 1, zero skips) in about 2.35 seconds without changing any startup, CPU, hang, or coverage budget. This remains a separate test-stability follow-up; no harness changes are included in the maintenance caller PR."
  "2026-10-14T12:59:25.805Z",codex-agent,"Additional reproduction: a second unchanged full npm gate passed 598/599 tests, with only extract-release failing to reach readiness within 5000 ms. No operation CPU-budget assertion failed. The failing operation differed from the first maintenance attempt, and the isolated startup control had passed. The harness and its deadlines remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-14T13:29:44.730Z",codex-agent,"Final maintenance validation: the complete npm gate passed all 599 tests without package-gate overlap; the complete Bun gate also passed 599/599. Both had zero failures and zero skips, with startup, operation CPU, hang, and coverage budgets unchanged. The two earlier npm startup failures remain useful reproductions, so this separate stability issue stays open; no harness or runtime changes were made."
  "2026-10-16T04:04:39.278Z",codex-agent,"Current-main audit at aafea5d (package 2026.10.15): Still open; larger harness change. `test/generator-redos.test.ts:9` still uses a 5000ms startup limit, separately from the 250ms parser CPU limit and 5000ms operation watchdog. Earlier load-sensitive readiness failures were not parser-budget failures. Passing gates do not invalidate that reproduction. See design below. Design: Extract the child-process harness into a test utility with distinct bounded startup, ready-to-command, and operation phases. Keep the 250ms parser CPU budget, every hostile input, and an independent finite operation watchdog. Choose and document a separate startup allowance using controlled loaded and unloaded runs; never retry or reset the operation CPU measurement to hide a parser failure. Add deterministic delayed-readiness, never-ready, worker-error, CPU-overrun, and post-ready hang cases. On every exit path terminate and await the child before resolving, so a timed-out probe cannot overlap the next one. Keep the full suite and coverage run as acceptance alongside the loaded/unloaded comparison. The lifecycle refactor and its negative controls exceed a small timeout edit; raising the single constant alone would leave them unverified.  No item is closed; verification and closure remain with the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-16T04:22:28.215Z",codex-agent,"Release-gate receipt on code commit 443ab9e: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed 610/610 tests, 49 suites, zero failures/cancelled/skipped/todo. Each used a fresh home with GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Both report exact 100% measured lines/branches/functions across 13 source files, 169 documented declarations, and passing production audit, package dry run, changelog/date and canonical attestation checks. Thresholds, source scope, CPU and worker startup/watchdog budgets are unchanged. Independent statements remain unmeasured; the known startup-readiness issue remains open. No item is closed."
  "2026-10-20T11:16:52.854Z",codex-agent,"Validation evidence from pmc-txk1 / PR 262 at code commit 51447ab: full isolated-HOME/Git npm release:check ran 682 tests, 671 pass and 11 fail; all 11 failures are the unchanged 5000ms worker-readiness deadline before the 250ms parser CPU operation. The full Bun run had the same 11 readiness failures plus a separate hostile-link timing assertion recorded on pmc-rspo. Both measured exact 100 percent lines/branches/functions. CI Node 22 and Node 26 on the same source each pass 682/682 and all release checks. Source hashes match before and after both local runs; no startup, operation CPU, watchdog, coverage threshold or input was changed. This is additional reproduction evidence, not a diagnosis of scheduler load or a fix; keep the readiness follow-up open."
  "2026-10-20T12:25:51.296Z",codex-agent,"PR 262 review validation reproduces startup-only failures under the unchanged full npm release gate on Node 26.12.0 with isolated HOME/Git configuration: 703/713 passed, 10 worker readiness timeouts at 5000ms, zero skipped/cancelled; the remaining ReDoS control passes. Coverage is 100 percent lines/branches/functions. No parser, startup or watchdog budget changed. The review-specific closure regressions pass within this run."
  "2026-10-20T12:52:54.558Z",codex-agent,"The complete Bun release:check control on the same unchanged source, Node 26.12.0 and isolated HOME/Git configuration with two CPUs available passes 712/713: one extract-release worker fails to start within 5000ms; all other ReDoS cases and hostile-Markdown wall-time controls pass. Zero skipped/cancelled. Measured lines/branches/functions remain 100 percent. Reducing concurrent files helps but does not eliminate the existing startup issue. No timing or coverage budget was changed."
  "2026-10-21T18:36:06.415Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced while validating tracker release milestones: the unchanged full coverage gate reported seven generator-redos worker startup failures at the 5000ms readiness deadline before operation execution. An isolated node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/generator-redos.test.ts run also reproduced readiness timeouts. The milestone feature tests passed 4/4 with 100% lines, branches and functions in the new module. Preserve this as a separate validation-harness follow-up; do not weaken the 250ms CPU budget or hang watchdog to land feature work."
